# Types

## Source of Truth

`types/api.ts` is the canonical source for all API/backend types. `types.ts` re-exports from `types/api.ts` and adds frontend-only display models.

```typescript
// types.ts — re-exports canonical types
export type { Order, Thread, Stage, CompanyField, ... } from './types/api';

// Frontend-only types defined here
export interface ChatSession { ... }
export interface Message { ... }
```

## Rules

- Never duplicate a type that already exists in `types/api.ts`.
- New backend response types go in `types/api.ts`.
- New frontend display models go in `types.ts`.
- Shared utility types go in `shared/index.ts`.
